# Data rules

- Store timestamps as `timestamptz` in UTC. Never shift a stored timestamp to fake the user's day.
- Compute "today" and "yesterday" at read time. A user's day runs from `day_start_time` in their IANA timezone until the same hour on the next date. If local time is earlier than that hour, the instant belongs to the previous date.
- Set `last_touched_at` to `created_at` on insert. Update it only when the user edits content, edits the optional note on a link/image/voice item, changes status, changes category, adds or removes a tag, or presses Revive.
- Opening a card, loading a list, playing audio, and rendering revival are not touches. Revival does not change `created_at` or `status`.
- New items start as `inbox` with `category_id` null. Assigning a category does not change status.
- Entering `done` writes a `done` ClearEvent. Leaving `done` removes that event if it falls in the current user-day. Permanent delete writes a `deleted` event that stays. Archive writes nothing.
- Store email trimmed and lowercased. Names for categories and tags are unique per user, case-insensitive.
- One image item holds one image (max 5 MB). One voice item holds one clip (10 minutes or 15 MB). Keep the recorded blob. Do not transcode.
